      "3 + (−6)",
      "6 − 3"
     ],
     "after": "Subtracting 6 is the same as adding −6. So 3 − 6 = 3 + (−6) = −3.",
     "ref": "Activity 2.4.2 Q1",
     "id": "g7.maths.u2.s2-4.22"
    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "Definition: subtraction",
     "paras": [
      "Subtracting b from a is the same as adding the opposite of b to a.",
      "For any integers a and b: a − b = a + (−b)."
